Key Capabilities Verified:
1. Shift Claim Preconditions & Locking (Part 6.7):
   - Roster check: Driver must have active roster entry (valid_from <= now <= valid_to) for bus; unrostered driver rejected with NOT_ROSTERED.
   - Bus mutual exclusion: At most one ACTIVE shift per bus. Second driver attempting to claim same bus rejected with BUS_SHIFT_ALREADY_ACTIVE.
   - Driver mutual exclusion: Driver already on active shift cannot start concurrent shift on another bus (DRIVER_ALREADY_ON_SHIFT).
   - Issues shift claim containing shift_id, bus_id, driver_id, route_id, trip_id, started_at.
   - Shift end lifecycle: POST /api/v1/shifts/end transitions status to COMPLETED; once ended, claim stops allowing telemetry uploads.
2. Driver Phone Ingestion Pipeline (Part 5.3 & SW-MVP section 11.7):
   - Auth & scope: Authenticated via driver context with active shift; non-existent or completed shifts reject uploads with 401/403.
   - Sample attribution: Attributed directly to the shift's bus_id (phone attribution is shift-bound, not via device link).
   - Speed conversion: speed_mps converted to km/h (multiplied by 3.6).
   - Adaptive cadence: Response returns phone_interval_s = 30s in Standby mode (HW active), and 10s in Fallback mode (PHONE active).
   - Mock filter (C-03 / C-10): Samples with is_mock = true are rejected from live state (MOCK_LOCATION) and stored with flag; never update live state.
   - Conflict handling (C-09 / OV-1): Duplicate sample sequence with conflicting payload rejected with per-sample HTTP 200 { seq, reason: 'CONFLICT' }; identical duplicates accepted silently.
   - Provider & accuracy filter: Samples with provider = NETWORK or accuracy_m > 50 rejected from live tracking.
   - Driver diagnostics: POST /api/v1/driver/status records OS, permissions (location, notifications), battery %, network type, and background execution state.
